  "note": "Splits the two registers Malcolm asked for. The small nav tiles at the top get a uniform product-on-white hero; the large detail sections below get the product IN USE - pipette lifted clear with a drop forming for the serums, jar open with the lid beside it or a swatch for the creams. Previously both rows used the same image, which is what made the page look flat.\n\nTHREE COMPROMISES, none of them hidden:\n  * Matrixyl 3000 SERUM has no white-background hero anywhere - not in live media, not in the local finals. It falls back to its pedestal-edge hero, which sits on teal.\n  * Matrixyl Firming CREAM likewise - its gradient hero, also teal.\n  * Copper Peptide SERUM has no pipette-pulled-out frame. The macro dropper-tip gel pour was tried first and rejected on sight: it is an extreme macro of gel leaving the pipette with NO BOTTLE IN SHOT, so it reads as an abstract texture rather than a product. Replaced with hands_only_dropper_4, one of Malcolm's published picks, which shows the bottle with the pipette lifted clear and a drop forming on a fingertip - the register he actually asked for.\nThe two teal tiles break exactly the uniformity that was asked for. Generating a white-background hero for those two products is the real fix and is not done here.\n\nOne more worth recording: the Copper Day Gel-Cream white hero is UNMARKED in the finals folder - Malcolm marks keepers with a leading underscore and publishes with two, and this file has neither. It is the only white-background frame that product has, so it is used, but he has never actually chosen it.",
